{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f34414621e164e4c08b7248f1bb96655b5dbc2567205a6ae232e9349e4b7af28","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI/CD workflow gate guards","key_entities":[".github/workflows/test.yml","gerrit-verify.yaml","scripts/check_readme_quickstart.py","scripts/probe_rebar.py","tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py","test_completeness_every_gate_step_is_guarded_or_marked","test_empty_tree_every_guarded_step_skips_cleanly","test_golden_path_guards_match_the_verified_lane"],"problem_keywords":["gate guard","predates gate","workflow","parity","test.yml","golden-path","script guard"],"propositions":["test.yml's golden-path job runs two scripts without predates-gate guards, whereas gerrit-verify.yaml guards the same scripts, causing spurious failures when a change predates the script.","The Verified lane and mirror lane must maintain parity: both script invocations must be guarded with the canonical `[ ! -f <path> ]` check and skip message.","Acceptance criteria require both guarded steps to carry -f guards naming their scripts, pass the parity completeness and empty-tree tests, and limit diffs to only those two steps.","The gap was latent from an earlier commit that predates the guard obligation, fixed only in gerrit-verify.yaml but not in test.yml."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787725096608509001,"uuid":"0f1e4811-8de9-4d9c-963f-80ef6b22f94f"}